    "updated_at": "2025-09-13T18:27:20Z",
    "body": "Thank you so much for the fix!\n\nUnfortunately I have a follow up - it did seem to fix the issue, both in the original code and in mine. However, it now raises a new one when running on my code, perhaps because of the number of dimensions:\n`RuntimeError: permute(sparse_coo): number of dimensions in the tensor input does not match the length of the desired ordering of dimensions i.e. input.dim() = 4 is not equal to len(dims) = 3`\n\nTo reproduce the error:\n```\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nfrom phi.torch.flow import *\nimport phiml.math as math\n\nMinimal CNN model for demonstration\nclass MinimalCNN(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.conv1 = nn.Conv2d(3, 16, 3, padding=1)\n        self.conv2 = nn.Conv2d(16, 2, 3, padding=1)\n        self.relu = nn.ReLU()\n        \n    def forward(self, x):\n        x = self.relu(self.conv1(x))\n        x = self.conv2(x)\n        return x\n\n\ndef step(v, p, cylinder, dt=1.0):\n    \"\"\"Single simulation step\"\"\"\n    v = advect.semi_lagrangian(v, v, dt)\n    v, p = fluid.make_incompressible(v, cylinder, Solve(x0=p,\n                                                     method='CG',\n                                                     rel_tol=0.01,\n                                                     max_iterations=2500))\n    return v, p\n\n\n# Setup\ndevice = torch.device('cpu')\n\n# Create model\nmodel = MinimalCNN()\noptimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\nloss_fn = nn.MSELoss()\n\n# Create cylinder obstacle\ncylinder = geom.Sphere(x=0.5, y=0.5, radius=0.1)\n\n# Create dummy data\nbatch_size = 10\nresolution = 64\n\nX_batch = torch.randn(batch_size, 3, resolution, resolution)\n\n# Dummy target: [batch, 2, height, width] - velocity field\ny_batch = torch.randn(batch_size, 2, resolution, resolution)\n\n# Dummy initial velocity: [batch]\nv0_batch = torch.randn(batch_size)\n\n# Forward pass\noptimizer.zero_grad()\nv0 = model(X_batch)  # [batch, 2, height, width]\n\n# Convert to PhiFlow format\ninitial_velocities = math.tensor(v0_batch, batch('batch'))\n\n# Set up boundary conditions\nboundaries = {\n    'x': PERIODIC,  # Periodic in x-direction\n    'y+': vec(x=0, y=-initial_velocities),  # Inflow from top\n    'y-': ZERO_GRADIENT  # Zero gradient outflow at bottom\n}\n\n# Create StaggeredGrid\nv0_field = StaggeredGrid(\n    math.tensor(v0, batch('batch'), channel('vector'), spatial('x,y')),\n    boundaries, \n    x=resolution, y=resolution, \n    bounds=Box(x=1, y=1)\n)\n\nv0_field, p0 = fluid.make_incompressible(\n    v0_field, \n    cylinder, \n    Solve('CG', rel_tol=0.01, max_iterations=2500)\n)\n\n\n# Simulate one step\nv_current, p_current = v0_field, p0\nv_current, p_current = step(v_current, p_current, cylinder, dt=.1)\n\n# Extract back to tensor\nvt = v_current.values.native('batch,~vector,x,y')\n\n# Compute loss\nloss = loss_fn(vt, y_batch)\nloss.backward()\noptimizer.step()\nprint(f\"Loss: {loss.item()}\")\n```\n\nAgain any help will be much appreciated 🙏🏼",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
